WEBVTT

00:00.211 --> 00:02.294
- [Instructor] We're told consider the sum

00:02.294 --> 00:05.399
two plus five plus eight plus 11.

00:05.399 --> 00:09.046
Which expression is
equal to the sum above?

00:09.046 --> 00:12.435
And they tell us choose
all answers that apply.

00:12.435 --> 00:13.943
So like always, pause the video,

00:13.943 --> 00:16.814
and see if you can work
through this on your own.

00:16.814 --> 00:18.178
So when you look at the sum,

00:18.178 --> 00:20.037
it's clear you're starting at two.

00:20.037 --> 00:23.148
You're adding three each time.

00:23.148 --> 00:25.975
And we also are dealing with

00:25.975 --> 00:28.401
you have four total terms.

00:28.401 --> 00:30.605
Now we could try to
construct an equation here

00:30.605 --> 00:32.909
or an expression using sigma notation.

00:32.909 --> 00:35.229
But instead, what I like to
do, is look at our options.

00:35.229 --> 00:37.783
We really only have to look
at these two options here

00:37.783 --> 00:39.226
and expand them out.

00:39.226 --> 00:41.873
What sum would each of these be?

00:41.873 --> 00:43.673
Well, this is going to be the same thing

00:43.673 --> 00:45.649
as we're starting at n equals one.

00:45.649 --> 00:48.714
So this is going to be three
times, when n equals one,

00:48.714 --> 00:50.745
three times one minus one.

00:50.745 --> 00:54.035
And then plus, then
we'll go to n equals two.

00:54.035 --> 00:56.202
Three times two minus one.

00:57.135 --> 00:59.262
Then we're gonna go to n equals three.

00:59.262 --> 01:02.262
So plus three times three minus one.

01:03.486 --> 01:06.138
And then finally, we're
gonna go to n equals four.

01:06.138 --> 01:08.777
So plus three times, when n equals four,

01:08.777 --> 01:12.002
this is three times four minus one.

01:12.002 --> 01:16.126
So just to be clear, this is
what we did when n equals one.

01:16.126 --> 01:16.959
Let me write it down.

01:16.959 --> 01:18.287
N equals one.

01:18.287 --> 01:22.170
This is what we got when n equals two.

01:22.170 --> 01:26.002
This is what we got when n equals three.

01:26.002 --> 01:30.002
And this is what we got
when n is equal to four.

01:31.434 --> 01:33.667
And we stopped at n equals four

01:33.667 --> 01:35.692
'cause it tells us right over there,

01:35.692 --> 01:36.663
we start at n equals one

01:36.663 --> 01:38.568
and we go all of the way to n equals four.

01:38.568 --> 01:40.218
So what does this equal?

01:40.218 --> 01:44.072
So let's see, three times
one minus one is two.

01:44.072 --> 01:45.978
So this is looking good so far.

01:45.978 --> 01:48.587
Three times two minus one,

01:48.587 --> 01:49.938
that's six minus one.

01:49.938 --> 01:51.279
That is five.

01:51.279 --> 01:52.810
So still looking good.

01:52.810 --> 01:56.047
Three times three minus
one, that's nine minus one.

01:56.047 --> 01:58.059
Once again, still looking good.

01:58.059 --> 02:00.487
Three times four minus one,

02:00.487 --> 02:01.404
that is 11.

02:02.365 --> 02:03.629
So we like this choice,

02:03.629 --> 02:05.714
so I would definitely select this one.

02:05.714 --> 02:08.197
Now let's do the same thing over here.

02:08.197 --> 02:10.197
When n is equal to zero,

02:11.345 --> 02:15.379
it's going to be two
plus three times zero.

02:15.379 --> 02:17.177
So that's just going to be two.

02:17.177 --> 02:20.107
And then plus, when n is equal to one,

02:20.107 --> 02:23.059
it's going to be two plus three times one,

02:23.059 --> 02:24.032
which is five.

02:24.032 --> 02:25.474
This is starting to look good.

02:25.474 --> 02:28.028
Now when n is equal to,
this was n equals zero,

02:28.028 --> 02:29.129
this was n equals one,

02:29.129 --> 02:30.925
so now we're at n equals two.

02:30.925 --> 02:32.367
So at n equals two,

02:32.367 --> 02:34.367
two plus three times two

02:35.570 --> 02:38.503
is two plus six, which is eight.

02:38.503 --> 02:39.336
And this makes sense.

02:39.336 --> 02:42.511
Every time we increase n by one,

02:42.511 --> 02:45.135
we are adding another three,

02:45.135 --> 02:46.606
which is consistent
with what we saw there.

02:46.606 --> 02:48.702
We start at two, when n equals zero,

02:48.702 --> 02:50.822
this is just, that three n is just zero.

02:50.822 --> 02:52.556
So you start at two, and then you keep,

02:52.556 --> 02:55.094
every time you increase n by one,

02:55.094 --> 02:56.943
you are just adding three again.

02:56.943 --> 02:58.727
So finally, when n is equal to three,

02:58.727 --> 03:02.370
two plus three times three is two plus,

03:02.370 --> 03:03.845
or is

03:03.845 --> 03:05.538
11, I should say.

03:05.538 --> 03:08.731
And so this also is exactly the same sum.

03:08.731 --> 03:12.137
So I feel good about both of these.

03:12.137 --> 03:14.304
Let's do one more example.

03:15.962 --> 03:18.102
So we're here, we're given the sum,

03:18.102 --> 03:19.711
and we're saying choose one answer.

03:19.711 --> 03:22.881
Which of these is equivalent
to this sum right over here?

03:22.881 --> 03:25.556
Well, like we did before,
let's just expand it out.

03:25.556 --> 03:28.562
And what's different here is
that we just have a variable,

03:28.562 --> 03:31.430
but that shouldn't make it
too much more difficult.

03:31.430 --> 03:33.299
So let's do the situation,
and I'll write it out.

03:33.299 --> 03:35.901
Let's do the situation
when n is equal to one.

03:35.901 --> 03:40.823
When n is equal to one, it's
gonna be k over one plus one.

03:40.823 --> 03:43.897
K over one plus one,
and I'll write it out.

03:43.897 --> 03:45.894
This is n is equal to one.

03:45.894 --> 03:48.469
And then plus, when n is equal to two,

03:48.469 --> 03:50.206
it's gonna be k

03:50.206 --> 03:51.706
over two plus one.

03:52.695 --> 03:55.113
This is n is equal to two.

03:55.113 --> 03:56.240
And then we're gonna keep going.

03:56.240 --> 03:57.741
When n is equal to three,

03:57.741 --> 03:59.544
it's gonna be k

03:59.544 --> 04:01.211
over three plus one.

04:02.317 --> 04:04.459
That's n is equal to three.

04:04.459 --> 04:05.987
And then plus, finally,

04:05.987 --> 04:09.151
'cause we stop right over
here at n equals four,

04:09.151 --> 04:13.318
when n equals four, it's going
to be k over four plus one.

04:14.968 --> 04:17.150
That's when n is equal to four.

04:17.150 --> 04:18.843
So this is all going to be equal,

04:18.843 --> 04:19.910
I'll just write it over here,

04:19.910 --> 04:22.935
this is equal to k over two,

04:22.935 --> 04:24.435
plus k over three,

04:25.586 --> 04:27.003
plus k over four,

04:28.743 --> 04:30.970
plus k over five,

04:30.970 --> 04:34.303
which is exactly this choice right over,

04:35.930 --> 04:37.395
right over here.

04:37.395 --> 04:39.600
And actually, if I had looked
at the choices ahead of time,

04:39.600 --> 04:41.512
I might have even been
able to save even more time

04:41.512 --> 04:43.832
by just saying, well, look,

04:43.832 --> 04:45.939
actually, if you just try
to compute the first term,

04:45.939 --> 04:48.655
when n is equal to one,
it would be k over two.

04:48.655 --> 04:52.140
Well, only this one is
starting with a k over two.

04:52.140 --> 04:55.695
This, this one has no k's
here, which is sketchy.

04:55.695 --> 04:57.137
They're trying to look at the error

04:57.137 --> 05:00.422
where you try to replace the
k with the number as well,

05:00.422 --> 05:01.361
not just the n.

05:01.361 --> 05:03.017
So that's what they're trying to do here.

05:03.017 --> 05:05.719
Here they're trying to, let's see,

05:05.719 --> 05:10.091
well, this isn't as obvious
what they're even trying to do,

05:10.091 --> 05:12.619
right over here where they
put the k in the denominator.

05:12.619 --> 05:15.369
And here if you swapped the n and the k's,

05:15.369 --> 05:17.682
then you would've gotten
this thing right over here.

05:17.682 --> 05:20.524
So we definitely feel good about choice A.
